{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"2498","artifact_type":"codebase-analysis","name":"plan/codebase-conventions-backlog-core-decompose.md@sha256:2873c6414b3f808685f7afbb3d0a4991e6e07a3274d08d8c421216618a2f1690"},"owner_reference":"2498","content":"# Codebase Conventions Analysis \u2014 backlog_core Decomposition (#2498)\n\nAnalysis date: 2026-09-03  \nTarget modules: `operations.py` (5,407 lines), `server.py` (4,640 lines)  \nExtraction targets: `section_filter.py`, `view_assembly.py`, `view_budget.py`\n\n---\n\n## 1. Precedent: Module Decomposition with Re-Export Stubs\n\n**Pattern Exists: YES**\n\nThis codebase ALREADY USES the \"split large module into siblings with re-export stubs\" pattern in two established locations.\n\n### Pattern 1: backlog_core Package Level\n\n**File:** `backlog_core/__init__.py` (lines 1-24)\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom ._branch_delegates import (\n    create_integration_branch,\n    delete_integration_branch,\n    get_integration_branch_status,\n    list_integration_branches,\n    merge_integration_branch,\n)\nfrom .models import BranchConflictError, BranchInfo, MergeResult\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"BranchConflictError\",\n    \"BranchInfo\",\n    \"MergeResult\",\n    \"create_integration_branch\",\n    \"delete_integration_branch\",\n    \"get_integration_branch_status\",\n    \"list_integration_branches\",\n    \"merge_integration_branch\",\n]\n```\n\n**Characteristics:**\n- Private implementation module: `_branch_delegates.py` (leading underscore)\n- Public re-export stub in `__init__.py`\n- Explicit `__all__` list controls what is publicly available\n- Models kept separate in `models.py`, imported alongside implementation functions\n- Pattern established: `from ._internal_module import public_names`\n\n### Pattern 2: sam_schema Package Level\n\n**File:** `sam_schema/__init__.py` (lines 1-96)\n\nRe-exports from nested modules (`core.models`, `core.query`, `readers.detect`, `writers.yaml_writer`) with explicit `__all__` collecting all public names at package level.\n\n**Characteristics:**\n- Multi-level decomposition: `core.models`, `core.query`, `readers.detect`, `writers.yaml_writer`\n- Docstring at module top documents the \"Public API\" and what is re-exported\n- All public names collected in a single `__all__` at package level\n- Imports use absolute paths (`sam_schema.core.models...`) not relative\n- Intermediate `sam_schema/core/__init__.py` is minimal (only quality gates)\n\n### Application to #2498\n\n**Establish re-export stub pattern in operations.py**\n\nAfter extracting `section_filter.py`, `view_assembly.py`, `view_budget.py` from `operations.py`:\n\n1. Create sibling modules as `_section_filter.py`, `_view_assembly.py`, `_view_budget.py` (leading underscore signals internal)\n2. Leave `operations.py` as a re-export stub for backward compatibility\n3. Add a docstring explaining the public API (following sam_schema pattern)\n4. Maintain explicit `__all__` exports (following backlog_core pattern)\n5. Use relative imports (`from ._section_filter import ...`) to keep the module dependency visible\n\n---\n\n## 2. Testing Conventions in backlog_core/tests/\n\n**Test file count:** 617 tests collected (pytest output)  \n**Test directory:** `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/`\n\n### Import Patterns Currently in Use\n\nTests use BOTH module-level and from-import styles interchangeably:\n\n#### Pattern A: Module-Level Import\n\n```python\nfrom backlog_core import operations\nfrom backlog_core.models import ViewItemResult\n\n# Usage\noperations._apply_body_section_filter(...)\n```\n\n#### Pattern B: From-Import (Specific Functions)\n\n```python\nfrom backlog_core.operations import _apply_body_section_filter, narrow_body_to_named_sections\n```\n\n**Files using these patterns:** `test_section_boundary_scanner_live_3152.py`, `test_view_pagination_section_index.py`, `test_view_section_form_resolution.py`\n\n### Fixture Patterns Observed\n\n**conftest.py** (`backlog_core/tests/conftest.py`, 80 lines):\n- Pre-warms `tiktoken` encoder cache before any test imports `server`\n- Defines a `_StubEncoder` class (inherits from `tiktoken.Encoding`)\n- Module-level `REAL_CL100K_AVAILABLE` flag for conditional test skipping\n- Purpose: prevent network calls during offline testing\n\n**Test-specific fixtures:**\n- `_view_test_helpers.py` provides mocking utilities (`_patch_github_body`, `_call_view`, `_resp_body`)\n- Fixtures are imported directly in test files, not via pytest `@pytest.fixture`\n\n### Test Import Behavior After Extraction\n\nWhen functions move from `operations.py` to `_section_filter.py` etc.:\n\n1. **Direct imports remain valid** (if operations.py re-exports):\n   ```python\n   from backlog_core.operations import apply_body_section_filter  # Still works\n   ```\n\n2. **Internal-module imports also work** (explicit about origin):\n   ```python\n   from backlog_core._section_filter import apply_body_section_filter\n   ```\n\n3. **Module-level access continues**:\n   ```python\n   from backlog_core import operations\n   operations.apply_body_section_filter(...)  # Still works\n   ```\n\n**No special testing protocol required** \u2014 the existing test suite structure supports moved functions transparently if `operations.py` re-exports.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Typing Conventions in operations.py and server.py\n\n### Type Foundation: Pydantic Models Preferred\n\n**Observation:** Both files use Pydantic `BaseModel` for structured data, not `@dataclass` or `TypedDict`.\n\n#### Pydantic Usage in server.py (authoritative example)\n\n```python\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, Field\n\n_ResponseModel = TypeVar(\"_ResponseModel\", bound=BaseModel)\n\nclass SyncStatusResponse(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Response schema for sync_status MCP tool.\"\"\"\n    # fields...\n```\n\nAll MCP tool response models inherit from `BaseModel`.\n\n### Type Aliases and Literals\n\n```python\nEffortLevel: TypeAlias = Literal[\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\", \"max\"]\nItemId: TypeAlias = int | str\n\nclass _SamTaskRow(TypedDict):\n    task_id: str\n    feature: str\n    status: str\n```\n\n**Observation:** TypedDict used for wire-level data shapes (JSON payloads from GitHub GraphQL), while Pydantic used for validated domain objects.\n\n### Imports and Annotations\n\n**operations.py imports (lines 1-85):**\n- `from typing import Any, Final, NotRequired, TypeGuard`\n- `from typing_extensions import TypedDict`\n- Pydantic models and domain objects from `.models`\n- Protocol types from `.backend_types` (ContentProvider, SyncProvider, etc.)\n\n**server.py imports (lines 1-50):**\n- `from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Annotated, Literal, TypeAlias, TypeVar`\n- `from pydantic import BaseModel, Field`\n- MCP-specific: `from mcp.types import ToolAnnotations`\n- `from fastmcp import Context, FastMCP`\n\n### Type Annotation Style\n\n**Consistent pattern:**\n- Use `from __future__ import annotations` (enables forward references)\n- Type hints on all public functions: `def fn(x: str) -> dict[str, Any]: ...`\n- Return type hints on ALL public functions (strict enforcement in CI)\n- Private functions: type hints required for parameters and return\n- No `Any` without justification\n\n---\n\n## 4. FastMCP Conventions in server.py\n\n### MCP Tool Registration Pattern\n\n**File structure:** `server.py` is a single FastMCP application file with module-level `mcp = FastMCP(...)` initialization.\n\nAll tools are registered via `@mcp.tool()` decorator on async functions.\n\n### Tool Definition Pattern\n\n```python\n@mcp.tool(\n    annotations=ToolAnnotations(\n        title=\"Human-Readable Tool Name\",\n        readOnlyHint=True|False,\n        destructiveHint=True|False,\n        idempotentHint=True|False,\n        openWorldHint=True|False,\n    )\n)\nasync def tool_name(\n    param1: Annotated[str, Field(description=\"...\")],\n    param2: Annotated[int, Field(description=\"...\", ge=0)],\n) -> ToolResponseModel:\n    \"\"\"Docstring describing the tool.\"\"\"\n    return _respond(ToolResponseModel, {\n        \"field1\": value1,\n        \"field2\": value2,\n    })\n```\n\n### Response Model Pattern\n\nAll MCP tools return Pydantic models. The `_respond()` helper (lines 146-191) validates payloads:\n\n```python\ndef _respond(\n    cls: type[_ResponseModel],\n    payload: Mapping[str, object],\n    *,\n    exclude_none: bool = True,\n    exclude_unset: bool = False,\n) -> _ResponseModel:\n    \"\"\"Validate a tool payload and return its wire dict.\"\"\"\n    return cls.model_validate(payload).model_dump(\n        exclude_none=exclude_none,\n        exclude_unset=exclude_unset\n    )\n```\n\n### Constraint: Tools Cannot Be Extracted from server.py\n\n**KEY LIMITATION:** MCP tool registration happens via `@mcp.tool()` decorator and module-level `mcp` object lifetime.\n\n**Consequence for #2498:**\n- `section_filter.py`, `view_assembly.py`, `view_budget.py` should contain ONLY internal helper functions\n- DO NOT move any `@mcp.tool()` decorated function to these modules\n- MCP tool functions MUST remain in `server.py`\n- Extracted modules provide pure functions (no MCP/FastMCP imports)\n\n---\n\n## 5. Implementation Recommendations\n\n### Module Naming Convention\n\nMatch established precedent: use private-module convention (leading underscore).\n\n- \u2705 Correct: `_section_filter.py`, `_view_assembly.py`, `_view_budget.py`\n- \u274c Incorrect: `section_filter.py` (would need explicit re-export, breaks precedent)\n\n### Re-Export Stub Maintenance\n\nAfter extraction, `operations.py` becomes a thin re-export facade:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"operations.py \u2014 Backlog CRUD operation facades (re-export stub).\n\nPublic functions extracted into focused modules:\n- _section_filter: View section filtering and assembly\n- _view_assembly: View composition and pagination\n- _view_budget: Token budget and pagination constraints\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom ._section_filter import (\n    # ... extracted functions ...\n)\nfrom ._view_assembly import (\n    # ... extracted functions ...\n)\nfrom ._view_budget import (\n    # ... extracted functions ...\n)\n\n__all__ = [\n    # explicit list of all public names\n]\n```\n\n### No test modifications required\n\nExisting test imports continue to work unchanged if `operations.py` re-exports.\n\n### Typing for Extracted Functions\n\n- Preserve type hints exactly as written in `operations.py`\n- Extract functions retain their original Pydantic model dependencies\n- New modules may import from `models.py` and `backend_types.py`\n- NO circular imports: extracted modules must not import from `server.py`\n\n---\n\n## Summary Table\n\n| Dimension | Finding | Application to #2498 |\n|-----------|---------|----------------------|\n| **Decomposition Pattern** | Exists and proven (backlog_core/__init__.py, sam_schema/__init__.py) | Use private module naming + re-export stub in operations.py |\n| **Test Conventions** | Both module-level and from-import supported; no migration needed | Existing 617 tests work unchanged |\n| **Typing** | Pydantic BaseModel primary; TypedDict for wire data; strict type annotations enforced | Preserve type hints; extracted functions return typed objects |\n| **FastMCP Constraint** | MCP tools must remain in server.py; cannot extract decorated functions | Keep all @mcp.tool functions in server.py; extract only helper functions |\n| **Re-Export Pattern** | Explicit __all__ + docstring at package level | Document extracted modules' purpose in operations.py docstring |\n"}